---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro'
import Code from '../../components/Code.astro'
import { to } from '../../data/paths.js'
const headings: [string, string][] = [['download', 'Download a file'], ['import', 'Import it'], ['update', 'Update later']]
---
<Docs title="Install: proof" description="Copy one file into your project. No package, no build step." slug="install" headings={headings}>
  <h1 class="plain">Install</h1>
  <p class="lead">Each library is one JavaScript module. Put it in your project and import it.</p>

  <h2 id="download">Download a file</h2>
  <p>Every library page has a download command. This one fetches ink:</p>
  <div class="cmd"><code data-curl={to('/r/ink.js')}>curl -O {to('/r/ink.js')}</code><button type="button" class="code-act" data-copy><i class="ic" aria-hidden="true">&#xF0C5;</i><span>copy</span></button></div>
  <p>You can also copy the source from the bottom of any library page.</p>

  <h2 id="import">Import it</h2>
  <p>The files are standard ES modules. They work in a plain script tag, and in any bundler such as Vite, Astro or Next.js.</p>
  <Code lang="html" name="index.html" code={`<script type="module">
  import { ink } from './ink.js'
  ink(document.querySelector('h1'))
</script>`} />

  <h2 id="update">Update later</h2>
  <p>The file is yours, so updates never arrive on their own. Read the <a href={to('/changelog')}>changelog</a>, then download the file again if you want the change. If you edited your copy, compare it with the new one first.</p>
</Docs>
